# SQL Setup Scripts

IMPORTANT: This directory contains scripts for setting up development databases only.
For production environments, use Alembic migrations (see scheduler/alembic/).

## Purpose

These SQL files are designed to:
1. Set up a fresh development database quickly
2. Provide a reference for the complete database schema
3. Import synthetic test data for development

## Important: Historical Data Required

The historical data is required for creating the development database and is not
included in the repo. You must overwrite the various syntheticfiles that are used
as placeholders in this directory such 003-import-data.sql.

## Usage

To set up a development database:

```bash
# Start fresh (drops existing database)
DROP_DB=true bash 000-run-migrations.sh

# Try to run migrations on existing database
bash 000-run-migrations.sh
```

## Important Notes

1. **Development Only**: These scripts are NOT meant for migrating live/production databases.
   Use Alembic migrations for production schema changes.

2. **Schema Management**:
   - The canonical schema is defined in SQLAlchemy models
   - These SQL files are derived from those models
   - Always update the models first, then regenerate these files
   - For live database changes, use Alembic migrations

## File Structure

- `000-run-migrations.sh`: Main setup script
- `001-schema.sql`: Base schema definition
- `[000-999]-*.sql`: Ordered migration files
- `*.sample.sql`: Example data files

## Additional Tools

- `generate-schemapdf.sh`: Creates a PDF of the ER diagram from schema.er
  (Requires the 'erd' tool to be installed)

For production deployments and schema changes, refer to the Alembic
migration documentation in scheduler/alembic/.

N.B. the database schema should be managed by Alembic to support schema
migrations of a live database. Currently the SQLAlchemy models fully capture the
schema represented by the files in this directory.

This directory contains the schema for the scheduler.. It is primarily intended
for reproduction of a development database not schema migrations of a live
database. It will only work for building the new database out of the old
database.

The generate-schemapdf.sh command turns schema.er into a pdf of a simplified ER diagram using the erd tool. If it is not installed the script will not run.
